From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-B3-002
Subject: [PATCH] MMAPI Manager: use truthful RG35XX media capabilities

--- a/src/javax/microedition/media/Manager.java
+++ b/src/javax/microedition/media/Manager.java
@@
 import org.recompile.mobile.Mobile;
 import org.recompile.mobile.PlatformPlayer;
 import org.recompile.mobile.JavaxPlatformPlayer;
 import org.recompile.mobile.SiemensPlatformPlayer;
+import org.recompile.mobile.RG35XXMediaProfile;
@@
 	public static String[] getSupportedContentTypes(String protocol)
 	{
 		Mobile.log(Mobile.LOG_DEBUG, Manager.class.getPackage().getName() + "." + Manager.class.getSimpleName() + ": " + "Get Supported Media Content Types");
-		return new String[]{"audio/midi", "audio/x-wav", "audio/x-mld",
-			"audio/amr", "audio/mpeg", "audio/x-tone-seq", "audio/mmf",
-			"audio/x-imy", "audio/basic" };
+		return RG35XXMediaProfile.getSupportedTypes(protocol);
 	}

Rationale:
- The generic FreeJ2ME list advertises codecs that are not proven on the
  JamVM/uClibc/native RG35XX path.
- Audited JARs may select media variants based on this list; false advertising
  can make a game choose AMR/MMF/MPEG instead of its MIDI/WAV alternatives.
- The target capability table remains intentionally conservative until a
  decoder/backend is proven on the RG35XX architecture.

Rollback:
Restore the original generic list only together with a target implementation
that actually supports every re-advertised type.
